# Rust
/target
/.debug
# Cargo.lock is committed. Every shared CI lane runs --locked -- clippy,
# cross-clippy, nextest and cargo publish -- which fails outright when the
# lockfile has to be created. It also pins what CI resolved, so a yanked or
# newly-published transitive dependency cannot turn a green tree red with no
# change to it. A lockfile in a library is ignored by downstream consumers.

